1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,471
You are then resolved to have him?

2
00:00:03,470 --> 00:00:05,469
to walk to Oakham Mount this morning.

3
00:00:06,369 --> 00:00:07,588
But I was embarrassed.

4
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:11,420
I assure you that I have long
been most heartily ashamed of it.

5
00:00:12,484 --> 00:00:14,240
Who are your uncles and aunts?

6
00:00:15,296 --> 00:00:17,742
What could your
ladyship propose by it?

7
00:00:18,524 --> 00:00:19,645
Indeed I had.

8
00:00:19,969 --> 00:00:21,400
Darcy, and Lizzy, and Kitty

9
00:00:22,252 --> 00:00:23,514
Collins well.

10
00:00:23,843 --> 00:00:25,262
You are joking, Lizzy.

11
00:00:25,568 --> 00:00:27,384
No, no, you shall not deceive me.

12
00:00:28,223 --> 00:00:30,399
did it soon make you
think better of me?

13
00:00:31,054 --> 00:00:34,157
Have you any idea, Lizzy,
who this gentleman is?

14
00:00:34,668 --> 00:00:36,218
Let me be rightly understood.

15
00:00:37,001 --> 00:00:38,940
I must beg to return to the house.

16
00:00:39,749 --> 00:00:42,715
Elizabeth again, and more
seriously assured her of its truth.

17
00:00:43,326 --> 00:00:45,294
I hope you are well, Miss Bennet.

18
00:00:46,217 --> 00:00:48,321
No indeed; I felt
nothing but surprise.

19
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:51,648
My dearest sister, now be serious.

20
00:00:52,570 --> 00:00:55,193
Will you tell me how
long you have loved him?

21
00:00:56,145 --> 00:00:57,417
Won't it, Kitty?

22
00:00:57,959 --> 00:01:01,271
I could not have parted with you,
my Lizzy, to anyone less worthy.

23
00:01:01,893 --> 00:01:04,540
And that I suppose is
one of your sisters.

24
00:01:04,955 --> 00:01:06,821
You have a very small park here

25
00:01:07,902 --> 00:01:10,794
Why, I must confess that I love
him better than I do Bingley.

26
00:01:11,944 --> 00:01:14,776
Go to your father, he
wants you in the library.

27
00:01:15,069 --> 00:01:16,757
A man who had felt less, might.

28
00:01:17,498 --> 00:01:19,427
This cannot be!--engaged to Mr.

29
00:01:20,431 --> 00:01:23,610
Let me know every thing that
I am to know, without delay.

30
00:01:23,993 --> 00:01:25,310
But the wife of Mr.

31
00:01:25,758 --> 00:01:28,407
Miss Bennet, I insist
on being satisfied.

32
00:01:29,432 --> 00:01:31,123
Darcy has never seen the view.

33
00:01:31,541 --> 00:01:32,801
And so was I.

34
00:01:33,786 --> 00:01:35,190
Now what have you to say?

35
00:01:35,938 --> 00:01:38,451
Elizabeth coloured and
laughed as she replied

36
00:01:39,097 --> 00:01:42,164
Has he, has my nephew, made
you an offer of marriage?

37
00:01:43,035 --> 00:01:45,675
Had you then persuaded
yourself that I should?

38
00:01:46,215 --> 00:01:47,471
MY DEAR LIZZY

39
00:01:48,211 --> 00:01:49,722
When I wrote that letter

40
00:01:50,370 --> 00:01:53,179
Tell me once for all,
are you engaged to him?

41
00:01:53,948 --> 00:01:57,467
You may ask questions which
I shall not choose to answer.

42
00:01:57,793 --> 00:02:00,466
How you must have hated
me after that evening?

43
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:03,500
I will make no promise of the kind.

44
00:02:04,371 --> 00:02:06,287
I am afraid you will be angry.

45
00:02:07,282 --> 00:02:10,191
But I have an aunt, too, who
must not be longer neglected.

46
00:02:11,186 --> 00:02:12,371
It taught me to hope

47
00:02:13,491 --> 00:02:15,359
Indeed, you are mistaken, Madam.

48
00:02:16,247 --> 00:02:18,827
Bennet, delighted to
speak to Lady Catherine.

49
00:02:19,216 --> 00:02:22,402
My dear Lizzy, where can
you have been walking to?
